  "content": [
    {
      "text": "death hath passed upon all men, to fulfil the merciful plan of the great Creator, 2 Ne. 9:6. how great the plan of our God, 2 Ne. 9:13. that cunning plan of the evil one, 2 Ne. 9:28 (D&C 10:12, 23). we know that thy plan was a very subtle plan, Alma 12:4. plan of redemption laid, which shall bring to pass the resurrection, Alma 12:25 (13:30; 34:16; 42:11). this being the plan of redemption which was laid, Alma 12:33. plan of redemption, which was prepared from the foundation of the world, Alma 22:13. according to the great plan of the Eternal God there must be an atonement, Alma 34:9. trust not those secret plans unto this people, Alma 37:32 (Hel. 2:6; 11:10, 26; Ether 8:9; 10:33). plan of restoration is requisite with the justice of God, Alma 41:2. plan of salvation would have been frustrated, Alma 42:5. temporal death … would destroy the great plan of happiness, Alma 42:8. plan of mercy could not be brought about except an atonement should be made, Alma 42:15. great plan of destruction … had been frustrated, 3 Ne. 1:16.",
